# CombatDOC UI Concept — Mobile-First Adaptive

The unit medic frequently works from a phone in the field. Every screen MUST
be built mobile-first and stay fully usable on a ~360–414px viewport. Desktop
is a progressive enhancement, never the baseline.

Full rationale and the visual system live in `docs/DESIGN.md`. This file is the
enforceable checklist — follow it whenever you touch `apps/web`.

## 1. Mobile-first, always

- Write base CSS for the phone. Add complexity upward with `min-width` media
  queries only. Do NOT write desktop styles first and patch them down with
  `max-width`.
- Standard breakpoints (aligned with the Ant / NG-ZORRO grid). Primary switch
  is `md` = 768px:
  - `xs` < 576, `sm` ≥ 576, `md` ≥ 768, `lg` ≥ 992, `xl` ≥ 1200.
- Never introduce horizontal page scroll on mobile. Content reflows vertically.

## 2. No data tables — ever

- Do NOT use `nz-table`, `<table>`, or fixed multi-column grids for data
  collections. They break on phones and are banned in this project.
- Render every collection as a vertical stack of card tiles using the shared
  classes in `apps/web/src/styles/_data.scss`:
  - Wrapper: `.tile-stack`
  - Item: `.data-tile` (+ modifiers: `--combat`, `--somatic`, `--muted`,
    `--error`, `--static`)
  - Parts: `.data-tile__head`, `__title`, `__action`, `__tags`, `__meta`,
    `__date`, `__diagnosis`, `__notes`
- Key/value detail data uses `.field-list` + `.field` chips (1 column on
  mobile, 2 at ≥640px, 3 at ≥1200px). Full-width values use `.field--wide`.
- On wide screens tiles MAY flow into a responsive multi-column grid, but the
  single-column mobile stack is the source of truth.

## 3. One canonical page scaffold for list screens

Use the shared `.page-list` scaffold from `_data.scss` for every list/index
screen. Do NOT invent per-feature container/header classes (e.g. the legacy
`.members-list-container` / `.page-header` pattern is deprecated):

- `.page-list` — root
- `.page-list__header` — title row + primary action (e.g. "Додати")
- `.page-list__filters` — search / date / status filters (wraps, full-width
  search on mobile)
- `.page-list__meta` — result count / hints
- `.page-list__pager` — centered `nz-pagination`

`apps/web/src/app/features/members/members-list.component.*` is the reference
implementation — mirror it for new list screens.

## 4. Touch ergonomics

- Interactive targets ≥ 44×44px on mobile. Avoid `nzSize="small"` for primary
  touch actions on phones.
- Phone numbers use `tel:` links; keep `(click)="$event.stopPropagation()"` on
  inline actions inside a clickable tile.
- Filters and header actions must `flex-wrap` and go full-width on mobile;
  never rely on a single non-wrapping row.
- Prefer a sticky/reachable primary action on long mobile screens.

## 5. Consult the NG-ZORRO demos before building a component

Before creating or substantially changing any NG-ZORRO-based component, check
the official demo for that component to use the exact, current Angular API and
markup (imports, module, selectors, inputs/outputs):

- Component gallery: https://ng.ant.design/components/overview/en
- Direct pattern, e.g. `https://ng.ant.design/components/modal/en`,
  `.../upload/en`, `.../form/en`, `.../list/en`, `.../tag/en`,
  `.../date-picker/en` — each demo page ships copy-pasteable Angular code.
- Match the version in `apps/web` (NG-ZORRO 17). Prefer the demo's imports and
  template shape over guessing an API from memory, and adapt it to the
  mobile-first conventions in this file.
- Note: `nz-table` demos exist on the site, but data collections in this
  project still use the card-tile pattern from section 2 — do not add tables.

## 6. Navigation

- Sidebar (`nz-sider`) collapses to a drawer/trigger under `md` (768px) — this
  is already wired in `core/layout`. Keep new nav entries working in the
  collapsed state (icon + label).

## 7. Forms & modals

- One column on mobile; multi-column only at ≥ `md` via the NG-ZORRO grid
  (`nz-row` / `nz-col` with responsive spans, not fixed widths).
- Modals are full-width on mobile: pass `nzWidth: '100%'` (or the existing
  `formModalWidth()` helper) below 768px; `.ant-modal` is already capped to
  `calc(100vw - 16px)` in `_data.scss`.

## 8. Theme constraints (do not regress)

- Keep the Ant Design Pro look defined in `theme.less` / `styles.scss`:
  Golden Purple primary `#722ED1`, Inter font, `uk_UA` locale, dates via
  `date-fns` (Ukrainian). Status colors: COMBAT = red, SOMATIC = blue,
  active = green, closed = gray.

## Definition of done (UI changes)

Before considering a UI change complete, confirm at a 360–414px width:
- no horizontal scroll,
- no table/grid squashing,
- all actions tappable and reachable,
- the screen uses `.page-list` + `.tile-stack` / `.field-list` conventions.
